A||N||15||gkozlov||Audio Question||||1||
Z||000000||gkozlov||09-13-2000||01:14 AM||||I have a Rockford Fosgate 8" sub which I would like to build a tube for. I have all the materials, but I dont know how to figure out how long the tube has to be cut. I know how to figure dimensions for a box, but how do I do it for a tube?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||Philphine||09-13-2000||01:45 AM||||radius squared times 3.14 times lenth of tube. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||GodSend||09-13-2000||01:08 PM||||  One cubic foot is 12 inchs * 12 inchs * 12 inchs , which is 1728 cubic inchs.<P>  To figure out the volume of a cylinder, its simply area * lenth, where area is "pie*radius*radius" - just measure the radius of the tube in inchs, .. lets say 5 inchs...(probably what you will want for a 8 in woofer, (an 8 inch woofer has a radius of 4 inchs))<P>3.14*5*5=78.5 cubic inchs.<P>if you make the tube 15 inchs long, you get<P>78.5*15 = 1177.5 cubic inchs...<P>to figure out how many cubic feet this is just divide the two like so..<P>1177.5/1728 = .68 cubic feet.<P>Hope this was not too confusing..<P><BR>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.hypernetcommunications.com/revn.gif">  <p>[This message has been edited by GodSend (edited 09-13-2000).]||||reg||3
Z||000003||Monkeyman||09-13-2000||08:26 PM||||Whew!  Making my brain smoke!  All I ever figured out was that 2 + 2 either equals 5 or the square root of pie divided by cake.||||reg||1
Z||000004||gkozlov||09-13-2000||10:17 PM||||Thanks to all those that responded. Monkeyman, thats exactly how I feel. I think Illgo ahead and start on it. Like I said it is a 8" Fosgate that requires between 0.3- 0.5 cubic feet of air space. The pipe im using is 8.5" PVC and MDF board. Im going to cut it 13" in length. That should give my the right amount of airspace. I was also told to stuff the tube with about a half a pound of pillow stuffing. Does any of this sound right? This is what Ive done so far. <A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/fiero_audio1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/fiero_audio1.htm</A>  <A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/install_photos.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/install_photos.htm</A> <BR>I want to repace that substation because of the amount of room it takes up.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sign1_3.jpg">  <BR><A HREF="http://g.kozlov.tripod.com/gkozlov.htm" TARGET=_blank>GKozlovs Fiero Site</A>||||reg||1
